    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303">

                <pb facs="0582" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg512"/>

                <head>No. 303.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 2, 1883</date>.
                        (Received July 3.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copy
                    of an approved report of a committee of the privy council of Canada, together
                    with copies of reports from the northwest mounted police force, relative to
                    certain hostilities between some Yankton Indians and half-breeds, which have
                    been forwarded to me by the Marquis of Lome, for the information of the United
                    States Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>





